{"id":"h19t2","name":"Nested Order Events","lang":"pyspark","entry":"solve","params":["spark","input_dir"],"limit_s":30,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The order service writes events as JSON Lines files (<code>.jsonl</code>, one JSON object per line) in <code>input_dir</code> and its sub-folders. Other files are ignored. A line looks like:</p>\n<pre>{\"order_id\": \"o1\", \"ts\": \"2026-03-02T10:00:00\", \"status\": \"paid\",\n \"customer\": {\"id\": \"c1\", \"country\": \"ma\"},\n \"items\": [{\"sku\": \"A\", \"qty\": 2, \"price\": 9.5}]}</pre>\n<p>Each event is the full state of the order at time <code>ts</code>; the same order can appear many times (created, paid, refunded...). Only the event with the <b>latest</b> <code>ts</code> of an order counts, and the order is counted only if that latest status is <code>\"paid\"</code>. Lines that are not valid JSON, or that have no <code>order_id</code> or no <code>ts</code>, are ignored. An order can have an empty <code>items</code> list.</p>\n<p>Country codes must be compared in upper case. Your task is to return, for each country with at least one counted order, the columns <code>country</code>, <code>orders</code> (long), <code>units</code> (long, total quantity), <code>revenue</code> (double, total of <code>qty * price</code>, rounded to 2 decimals) and <code>top_sku</code> (the sku with the highest total quantity in that country, the first in alphabetical order on a tie; <code>null</code> if the country has no item), sorted by <code>revenue</code> from the highest, then <code>country</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p class=\"exf\"><code>input_dir/day1/part-0.jsonl</code></p><pre class=\"exv\">{\"order_id\": \"o1\", \"ts\": \"2026-03-02T10:00:00\", \"status\": \"created\", \"customer\": {\"id\": \"c1\", \"country\": \"ma\"}, \"items\": [{\"sku\": \"A\", \"qty\": 2, \"price\": 9.5}]}\n{\"order_id\": \"o1\", \"ts\": \"2026-03-02T10:05:00\", \"status\": \"paid\", \"customer\": {\"id\": \"c1\", \"country\": \"ma\"}, \"items\": [{\"sku\": \"A\", \"qty\": 2, \"price\": 9.5}, {\"sku\": \"B\", \"qty\": 1, \"price\": 3.0}]}\n{\"order_id\": \"o2\", \"ts\": \"2026-03-02T11:00:00\", \"status\": \"paid\", \"customer\": {\"id\": \"c2\", \"country\": \"MA\"}, \"items\": [{\"sku\": \"B\", \"qty\": 3, \"price\": 3.0}]}\n{not json\n{\"order_id\": \"o3\", \"ts\": \"2026-03-02T12:00:00\", \"status\": \"paid\", \"customer\": {\"id\": \"c3\", \"country\": \"sn\"}, \"items\": []}\n</pre><p class=\"exf\"><code>input_dir/day2/part-0.jsonl</code></p><pre class=\"exv\">{\"order_id\": \"o2\", \"ts\": \"2026-03-03T09:00:00\", \"status\": \"refunded\", \"customer\": {\"id\": \"c2\", \"country\": \"MA\"}, \"items\": [{\"sku\": \"B\", \"qty\": 3, \"price\": 3.0}]}\n{\"order_id\": \"o4\", \"ts\": \"2026-03-03T09:00:00\", \"status\": \"paid\", \"customer\": {\"id\": \"c4\", \"country\": \"Sn\"}, \"items\": [{\"sku\": \"Z\", \"qty\": 1, \"price\": 100.0}, {\"sku\": \"Y\", \"qty\": 1, \"price\": 1.0}]}\n{\"order_id\": \"o5\", \"status\": \"paid\"}\n</pre><p class=\"exf\"><code>input_dir/day2/_SUCCESS</code></p><pre class=\"exv\"></pre><p class=\"exf\"><code>input_dir/day2/old.json</code></p><pre class=\"exv\">{\"order_id\": \"o9\", \"ts\": \"2026-03-04T00:00:00\", \"status\": \"paid\", \"customer\": {\"id\": \"c9\", \"country\": \"fr\"}, \"items\": [{\"sku\": \"A\", \"qty\": 9, \"price\": 9.0}]}</pre><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>country</th><th>orders</th><th>units</th><th>revenue</th><th>top_sku</th></tr><tr><td>SN</td><td>2</td><td>2</td><td>101.0</td><td>Y</td></tr><tr><td>MA</td><td>1</td><td>3</td><td>22.0</td><td>A</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 30 seconds (pyspark)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 2 GB<br><b>[input]</b> string input_dir (the path of a folder)<br><b>[output]</b> DataFrame with exactly the columns <code>country</code>, <code>orders</code>, <code>units</code>, <code>revenue</code>, <code>top_sku</code>, in this order; rows in the order given by the statement</div>","starter":"from pyspark.sql import SparkSession, DataFrame, functions as F\n\n\ndef solve(spark: SparkSession, input_dir: str) -> DataFrame:\n    # write your code here\n    return spark.read.json(input_dir)\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["consigne longue","JSON imbriqué","explode","dernière version par commande","lignes invalides","top par groupe"],"minutes":25,"source":"Kata Lab","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>solution.py</code>.</li><li>Complète la fonction <code>solve(spark, input_dir)</code>. Garde son nom et ses paramètres : ce sont les tests qui l'appellent, avec leurs propres données. N'écris pas d'appel à la fonction toi-même.</li><li><code>spark</code> est une SparkSession déjà prête : ne crée pas la tienne.</li><li><code>input_dir</code> est le <b>chemin d'un dossier</b> (une chaîne). Ses fichiers sont listés à gauche de l'éditeur sous <b>Files</b> : clique sur un fichier pour le lire (lecture seule), puis sur <code>solution.py</code> pour revenir à ton code. Lis les fichiers à partir de <code>input_dir</code>, jamais d'un chemin écrit à la main : chaque test donne un autre dossier.</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Ta fonction doit <b>renvoyer</b> le résultat avec <code>return</code>. Un <code>print</code> ou un <code>show()</code> ne compte pas : il sort seulement dans l'onglet <b>Console Output</b>.</li><li>Le DataFrame renvoyé doit avoir <b>exactement 5 colonnes</b>, avec ces noms et dans cet ordre : <code>country</code>, <code>orders</code>, <code>units</code>, <code>revenue</code>, <code>top_sku</code>. Une colonne en plus (une colonne de calcul oubliée), un nom différent ou un autre ordre et le test est faux, même si les valeurs sont justes. Finis par un <code>select(...)</code> de ces colonnes.</li><li><b>L'ordre des lignes compte</b> : trie exactement comme l'énoncé le demande (<code>orderBy</code> à la fin).</li><li>Valeurs : les nombres sont comparés à 0,000001 près : arrondis seulement là où l'énoncé le demande, et au nombre de décimales demandé.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Spark tourne dans ton Codespace : au premier RUN TESTS de la séance, attends qu'il soit prêt (1 à 2 minutes). Ensuite chaque lancement prend quelques secondes.</li><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : tes 2 tests visibles tournent.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 2/2. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 6 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":{"root":"input_dir","files":{"day1/part-0.jsonl":"{\"order_id\": \"o1\", \"ts\": \"2026-03-02T10:00:00\", \"status\": \"created\", \"customer\": {\"id\": \"c1\", \"country\": \"ma\"}, \"items\": [{\"sku\": \"A\", \"qty\": 2, \"price\": 9.5}]}\n{\"order_id\": \"o1\", \"ts\": \"2026-03-02T10:05:00\", \"status\": \"paid\", \"customer\": {\"id\": \"c1\", \"country\": \"ma\"}, \"items\": [{\"sku\": \"A\", \"qty\": 2, \"price\": 9.5}, {\"sku\": \"B\", \"qty\": 1, \"price\": 3.0}]}\n{\"order_id\": \"o2\", \"ts\": \"2026-03-02T11:00:00\", \"status\": \"paid\", \"customer\": {\"id\": \"c2\", \"country\": \"MA\"}, \"items\": [{\"sku\": \"B\", \"qty\": 3, \"price\": 3.0}]}\n{not json\n{\"order_id\": \"o3\", \"ts\": \"2026-03-02T12:00:00\", \"status\": \"paid\", \"customer\": {\"id\": \"c3\", \"country\": \"sn\"}, \"items\": []}\n","day2/part-0.jsonl":"{\"order_id\": \"o2\", \"ts\": \"2026-03-03T09:00:00\", \"status\": \"refunded\", \"customer\": {\"id\": \"c2\", \"country\": \"MA\"}, \"items\": [{\"sku\": \"B\", \"qty\": 3, \"price\": 3.0}]}\n{\"order_id\": \"o4\", \"ts\": \"2026-03-03T09:00:00\", \"status\": \"paid\", \"customer\": {\"id\": \"c4\", \"country\": \"Sn\"}, \"items\": [{\"sku\": \"Z\", \"qty\": 1, \"price\": 100.0}, {\"sku\": \"Y\", \"qty\": 1, \"price\": 1.0}]}\n{\"order_id\": \"o5\", \"status\": \"paid\"}\n","day2/_SUCCESS":"","day2/old.json":"{\"order_id\": \"o9\", \"ts\": \"2026-03-04T00:00:00\", \"status\": \"paid\", \"customer\": {\"id\": \"c9\", \"country\": \"fr\"}, \"items\": [{\"sku\": \"A\", \"qty\": 9, \"price\": 9.0}]}"}},"visible":[{"input":{"input_dir":{"__dir__":{"day1/part-0.jsonl":"{\"order_id\": \"o1\", \"ts\": \"2026-03-02T10:00:00\", \"status\": \"created\", \"customer\": {\"id\": \"c1\", \"country\": \"ma\"}, \"items\": [{\"sku\": \"A\", \"qty\": 2, \"price\": 9.5}]}\n{\"order_id\": \"o1\", \"ts\": \"2026-03-02T10:05:00\", \"status\": \"paid\", \"customer\": {\"id\": \"c1\", \"country\": \"ma\"}, \"items\": [{\"sku\": \"A\", \"qty\": 2, \"price\": 9.5}, {\"sku\": \"B\", \"qty\": 1, \"price\": 3.0}]}\n{\"order_id\": \"o2\", \"ts\": \"2026-03-02T11:00:00\", \"status\": \"paid\", \"customer\": {\"id\": \"c2\", \"country\": \"MA\"}, \"items\": [{\"sku\": \"B\", \"qty\": 3, \"price\": 3.0}]}\n{not json\n{\"order_id\": \"o3\", \"ts\": \"2026-03-02T12:00:00\", \"status\": \"paid\", \"customer\": {\"id\": \"c3\", \"country\": \"sn\"}, \"items\": []}\n","day2/part-0.jsonl":"{\"order_id\": \"o2\", \"ts\": \"2026-03-03T09:00:00\", \"status\": \"refunded\", \"customer\": {\"id\": \"c2\", \"country\": \"MA\"}, \"items\": [{\"sku\": \"B\", \"qty\": 3, \"price\": 3.0}]}\n{\"order_id\": \"o4\", \"ts\": \"2026-03-03T09:00:00\", \"status\": \"paid\", \"customer\": {\"id\": \"c4\", \"country\": \"Sn\"}, \"items\": [{\"sku\": \"Z\", \"qty\": 1, \"price\": 100.0}, {\"sku\": \"Y\", \"qty\": 1, \"price\": 1.0}]}\n{\"order_id\": \"o5\", \"status\": \"paid\"}\n","day2/_SUCCESS":"","day2/old.json":"{\"order_id\": \"o9\", \"ts\": \"2026-03-04T00:00:00\", \"status\": \"paid\", \"customer\": {\"id\": \"c9\", \"country\": \"fr\"}, \"items\": [{\"sku\": \"A\", \"qty\": 9, \"price\": 9.0}]}"}}},"expected":{"columns":["country","orders","units","revenue","top_sku"],"rows":[["SN",2,2,101.0,"Y"],["MA",1,3,22.0,"A"]]}},{"input":{"input_dir":{"__dir__":{"a.jsonl":"{\"order_id\": \"x\", \"ts\": \"2026-01-01T00:00:00\", \"status\": \"paid\", \"customer\": {\"id\": \"k\", \"country\": \"tg\"}, \"items\": [{\"sku\": \"B\", \"qty\": 2, \"price\": 1.0}, {\"sku\": \"A\", \"qty\": 2, \"price\": 1.0}]}\n"}}},"expected":{"columns":["country","orders","units","revenue","top_sku"],"rows":[["TG",1,4,4.0,"A"]]}}],"hidden_n":6,"hidden":"","solution":""}